From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] svg: add a resvg backend, with multi-glyph document support

Adds -Dsvg-backend=resvg, an OT-SVG backend using the resvg C
library. Unlike nanosvg, resvg can render a single element of a
document by its ID, so "multi-glyph" documents (one SVG document
holding many glyphs, each the element with id "glyph<index>") are
rendered correctly, instead of being rejected (fcft#120).

Parsed multi-glyph documents are cached, since they can be very large
(OpenMoji's picosvgz font has a single ~9MB document covering ~3700
glyphs).

Glyph scaling and placement mirrors the nanosvg backend.
---
 fcft.c              |  10 +-
 meson.build         |  14 ++
 meson_options.txt   |   4 +-
 svg-backend-resvg.c | 511 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 svg-backend-resvg.h |   6 +
 5 files changed, 542 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fcft.c b/fcft.c
